+What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../uke_charge_protection_state
+Date:           November 2026
+KernelVersion:  7.3.3
+Contact:        Uke kernel contributors
+Description:
+                Existing version-1 passive snapshot. Reads never request
+                firmware, acquire control, clear faults or change settings.
+                A stale/absent snapshot reports valid=0, not a fresh dry state.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../uke_charge_protection_observe_v2
+Date:           November 2026
+KernelVersion:  7.3.3
+Contact:        Uke kernel contributors
+Description:
+                Root-only (0400) read-only version-2 observation. A valid
+                five-second same-epoch cache avoids requests; otherwise two
+                fixed moisture GETs refresh it under the request mutex.
+                No SET, lease, timer, automatic retry or fault reset is added.
+                Errors remain errno; a partial GET does not become a record.
+
+                Fourteen decimal fields: version=2, instance, generation,
+                firmware epoch, source epoch, received boottime ns, detection
+                enabled, moisture, valid, wet latch, inhibit readback valid,
+                dry-since boottime ns, fault mask, GETs performed for this read.
+                The final flag is 0 for cache use and 1 after successful GETs;
+                an epoch race can still leave valid=0. It is not physical
+                moisture/thermal/cutoff qualification or actuator admission.
